<header class="page-hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">Fee management</span>
    <h1>One parent pays once, for every child</h1>
    <p class="lede" style="max-width:62ch">
      A father with three children in your school hands the clerk one bundle of
      cash. Most software makes the clerk do that three times, once per child,
      and prints three receipts. This does it once, and the receipt lists all
      three children with what each of them owed.
    </p>
    <div class="hero__cta">
      <a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href="/pricing" data-app="signup">Start 14 day free trial</a>
      <a class="btn btn--ghost btn--lg" href="/contact">Ask a question first</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="section section--tint">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>What a monthly fee run actually involves</h2>
    <p class="lede" style="margin-top:12px;max-width:64ch">
      Not "generate challans". These are the parts that take a clerk's morning,
      and the parts a spreadsheet gets wrong.
    </p>

    <div class="grid grid--2" style="margin-top:34px">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card__icon">
          <svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M4 6h16M4 10h16M4 14h16M4 18h16"></path></svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Fee heads and per class structures</h3>
        <p>Tuition, admission, exam, transport, whatever your school charges, each as its own head. Amounts are set per class, so class 9 and Play Group are not forced onto the same figure, and a change to next month's amounts does not rewrite last month's bills.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card__icon" style="background: var(--due-50); color: var(--due-800);">
          <svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 8v4l3 3m6-3a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"></path></svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Arrears that carry themselves forward</h3>
        <p>An unpaid month is not silently dropped when the next challan is issued. It is carried, it appears on the new challan as arrears, and the total a parent owes is one number rather than a stack of slips the office has to add up by hand.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card__icon card__icon--accent">
          <svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M11 3.055A9.001 9.001 0 1020.945 13H11V3.055z"></path><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M20.488 9H15V3.512A9.025 9.025 0 0120.488 9z"></path></svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Partial payments, and what is left</h3>
        <p>A parent pays Rs 2,000 of a Rs 5,800 bill. The receipt says so, the balance says so, and the next reminder is for the remainder rather than for the whole bill again. Nobody has to remember what was paid on the counter last Tuesday.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card__icon" style="background: var(--money-50); color: var(--money-700);">
          <svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M7 7h.01M7 3h5c.512 0 1.024.195 1.414.586l7 7a2 2 0 010 2.828l-7 7a2 2 0 01-2.828 0l-7-7A1.994 1.994 0 013 12V7a4 4 0 014-4z"></path></svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Discounts that somebody approved</h3>
        <p>A discount is not a number a clerk can type into a total. It is recorded against the pupil with a reason and the name of whoever allowed it, so a concession granted quietly is a concession you can find. Fines work the same way.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap split split--wide">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">Fee control</span>
      <h2>Know what should have been collected</h2>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-top:12px">
        Most school software tells you what was collected. That number is only
        useful if you already trust it. The harder and more valuable question is
        what the roll says should have arrived, and where the difference went.
      </p>
      <div class="note" style="margin-top:18px">
        <p>
          Nothing here is an accusation. Most of the gap in most schools is a
          mistake in the record, corrected by a reversal that leaves both entries
          in place with a reason and a name attached.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ul class="checklist" style="margin-top:22px">
        <li>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 10.5l4 4 8-9" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
          <span><b>Expected against collected:</b> class by class, from the real roll.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 10.5l4 4 8-9" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
          <span><b>Ghost student check:</b> anyone being billed who never appears in a register.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 10.5l4 4 8-9" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
          <span><b>Discounts need approval.</b> A clerk proposes, the principal approves, both are recorded.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 10.5l4 4 8-9" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
          <span><b>Gapless receipt numbers:</b> issued by the database, never by the person at the counter, so a missing one is visible.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 10.5l4 4 8-9" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
          <span><b>Full audit trail:</b> every change to money, marks and attendance, with who and when.</span>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="panel">
      <div class="panel__head">
        <span class="panel__title">Reconciliation</span>
        <span class="panel__sub">September 2026</span>
      </div>
      <div class="panel__body">
        <table class="recon">
          <caption class="sr">Expected against collected fee income by class</caption>
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Class</th><th>Expected</th><th>Collected</th><th>Gap</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Class 1</td><td>124,000</td><td>124,000</td><td class="ok">None</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Class 2</td><td>124,500</td><td>121,500</td><td class="short">3,000</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Class 3</td><td>132,000</td><td>96,000</td><td class="short">36,000</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Class 4</td><td>127,500</td><td>127,500</td><td class="ok">None</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div class="panel__foot">
        Class 3 is Rs 35,000 short. Eleven families are behind, and two students
        on the roll have never appeared in the attendance register.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tint">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Receipt numbers that cannot skip</h2>
    <p class="lede" style="margin-top:12px;max-width:64ch">
      Every receipt is issued in an unbroken sequence, and nothing is ever
      deleted. That single rule is what makes the rest of it checkable.
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top:16px;max-width:66ch">
      If a receipt could be deleted, a missing number would mean nothing: it could
      be a cancelled sale, a printer jam or cash that never reached the drawer, and
      there would be no way to tell which. Because a mistake is corrected by a
      <b>reversal</b> rather than a deletion, a gap in the sequence is always a
      question with an answer, and the answer is in the record with a name against
      it.
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top:20px">
      <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/guides/fee-challan-pakistan">What a fee challan has to say</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

